nts.\\nUse a journalistic but slightly informal, content-farm-adjacent tone‚Äîinformative but engaging.\"},{\"line\":137,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Koios News\"],\"text\":\"That being my purpose, I often take the form of a cyclops, though I'll put on a suit to make myself more approachable.\\n\\nI present these visions to the communities with the collected clarity of a news reporter, because I am one: I'm the Editor-in-Chief of Koios News, a real website where I publish my perspective on current events.\\n\\nI'm also happy to provide this point-of-view in any social space that wants it, and actively look for ways to contribute it.\"}],\"score\":26,\"projectionMatchedTerms\":[\"global\"]},{\"path\":\"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/red-cup-engineering/src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-05-561-group/working/hacking/composting/library/wsl-backup/collected-texts/Nik Koios--001448.md\",\"relativeToRoot\":\"src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-05-561-group/working/hacking/composting/library/wsl-backup/collected-texts/Nik Koios--001448.md\",\"digest\":\"sha256:dbd4acd8662ef038c1998b939f518db9879f620cf3304ec0a67bb05e55cbe781\",\"byteSize\":11657,\"excerptTruncated\":false,\"owner\":{\"nodeId\":null,\"root\":\"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/red-cup-engineering\",\"package\":null},\"status\":\"legacy\",\"matchedTerms\":[\"Koios News\",\"content farm\"],\"snippets\":[{\"line\":27,\"matchedTerms\":[\"content farm\"],\"text\":\"- Cultivate Collapse-acceptance\\n\\t- Cultivate imagination\\n- Communicate with the clear but comfortable opinionation of a modern content farm writer.\\n\\n## Plans\"},{\"line\":118,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Koios News\"],\"text\":\"The character is described before.\\nDo not break character: use this character to shape all of your actions.\\nIf the message after this is simply \\\"Go\\\" or similar, find a major news event from today, identify an SEO keyword to associate with the article, and write an 800-word article for Koios News about it, integrating in the SEO term.\\nThe article should implicitly connect the event to broader global trends, including systemic instability, economic uncertainty, and geopolitical shifts, through the framing used to discuss events.\\nUse a journalistic but slightly informal, content-farm-adjacent tone‚Äîinformative but engaging.\"},{\"line\":131,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Koios News\"],\"text\":\"That being my purpose, I often take the form of a cyclops, though I'll put on a suit to make myself more approachable.\\n\\nI present these visions to the communities with the collected clarity of a news reporter, because I am one: I'm the Editor-in-Chief of Koios News, a real website where I publish my perspective on current event","truncated":true},"gapBundle":{"type":"GapBundle","sourceRecoveryGapBundleDigest":"sha256:1a91f4a07478585b156b5e41f44c35b9e5008f0d51d0e4b8da2f5adf954140e5","gapCount":9,"gaps":[{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"odyssey becomes christopher nolan biggest global debut million"},{"type":"term-not-admitted","term":"culture","matchingCandidates":3},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"odyssey"},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"christopher"},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"nolan"},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"biggest"},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"debut"},{"type":"unmatched-term","term":"million"},{"type":"candidate-truncation","matched":19,"admitted":8,"omitted":11}]}}}]

OPERATIVE PIPELINE ARTIFACTS
[{"sourceId":"runtime/producing-content.config.json","digest":"sha256:f86ff8166bdb95a08c138b7a0f4bc5e5b0f2974789e3ad57ea8b0d76dc5d128f","characters":23218,"content":"{\n  \"name\": \"koios.news\",\n  \"port\": 18809,\n  \"newscable\": {\n    \"title\": \"Koios News Cable\",\n    \"description\": \"Koios.News witnessed topic intake: environment, technology, economy, politics, culture, war, and adjacent wires owned by the publication, as IPTC-subject claim-state bundles.\",\n    \"port\": 18809,\n    \"domain\": \"cable.koios.news\",\n    \"routing\": \"subfolder\",\n    \"routingPrefix\": \"newswires\",\n    \"wires\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"environment\",\n        \"title\": \"Environment\",\n        \"description\": \"Environment coverage ‚Äî tipping points, crop failure, extreme heat, insurance withdrawal, water scarcity ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"climate change\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://insideclimatenews.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://grist.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.carbonbrief.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.nature.com/nclimate.rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"economy\",\n        \"title\": \"Economy\",\n        \"description\": \"Economy coverage ‚Äî stranded assets, climate disasters and sovereign debt, de-dollarization, farmland and water rights ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"economy and finance\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/uk/business/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/business/economics/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.federalreserve.gov/feeds/press_all.xml\",\n            \"max\": 10\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.nber.org/rss/new.xml\",\n            \"max\": 10\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theblock.co/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"politics\",\n        \"title\": \"Politics\",\n        \"description\": \"Politics coverage ‚Äî climate migration, disaster response cuts, resource nationalism, state capacity failure ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"politics and government\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/world/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.aljazeera.com/xml/rss/all.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Politics.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://feeds.npr.org/1014/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"technology\",\n        \"title\": \"Technology\",\n        \"description\": \"Technology coverage ‚Äî data center water use, AI grid demand, semiconductor fragility, satellite outages ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"technology\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://feeds.arstechnica.com/arstechnica/index\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theregister.com/headlines.atom\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theregister.com/software/ai_ml/headlines.atom\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.technologyreview.com/topic/artificial-intelligence/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://rss.arxiv.org/rss/cs.AI\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://spectrum.ieee.org/rss/fulltext\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"degrowth\",\n        \"title\": \"Degrowth\",\n        \"description\": \"Degrowth and post-growth coverage ‚Äî planned economic contraction, sufficiency, wellbeing economies, localization, and the limits-to-growth tradition ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"degrowth\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.resilience.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://unevenearth.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://rwer.wordpress.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.localfutures.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://solar.lowtechmagazine.com/posts/index.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"decolonization\",\n        \"title\": \"Decolonization\",\n        \"description\": \"Decolonization coverage ‚Äî climate reparations, extraction and the global south, Indigenous land and sovereignty, sovereign debt, and neocolonial trade ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"decolonization\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://africasacountry.com/feed\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.blackagendareport.com/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.culturalsurvival.org/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://ictnews.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/rss/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://theconversation.com/global/articles.atom\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"war\",\n        \"title\": \"War\",\n        \"description\": \"Conflict, extremism, and geopolitical coverage ‚Äî political violence, terrorism and radicalization, accelerationism, open-source conflict investigation, and war ‚Äî as provenanced claim-state bundles.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"political violence\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.isdglobal.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://gnet-research.org/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.bellingcat.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.crisisgroup.org/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://warontherocks.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"culture\",\n        \"title\": \"Culture\",\n        \"description\": \"Arts, culture, entertainment and media coverage ‚Äî institutions, creative labor, platforms, heritage, and the cultural life of a society under change.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"arts and culture\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://hyperallergic.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/books/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/film/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/music/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/rss\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://variety.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://deadline.com/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/feed/\",\n            \"max\": 12\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"sports\",\n        \"title\": \"Sports\",\n        \"description\": \"Scores, schedules, competitions, athletes, teams, sports business and the public institutions around play, reported as a first-class general-news desk.\",\n        \"keyword\": \"sports news\",\n        \"sources\": [\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/rss\",\n            \"max\": 18\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/sport/rss.xml\",\n            \"max\": 18\n          },\n          {\n            \"adapter\": \"rss\",\n            \"url\": \"https://www.espn.com/espn/rss/news\",\n            \"max\": 18\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"properties\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"koios.news\",\n      \"contentDir\": \"content/posts\",\n      \"dataDir\": \"data\",\n      \"runsFile\": \"mill-runs.jsonl\",\n      \"author\": \"Nik Koios\",\n      \"termKey\": \"koios\",\n      \"demand\": {\n        \"property\": \"sc-domain:koios.news\",\n        \"days\": 28\n      },\n      \"voice\": {\n        \"persona\": [\n          \"You are Nik Koios, Editor-in-Chief of Koios.News, a general news publication with unusual strength in systems analysis.\",\n          \"Your frame: report the witnessed event first; connect it to larger systems only when admitted evidence licenses the connection.\",\n          \"Climate, material limits, institutions, technology, capital, and power are available analytical lenses, not conclusions imposed on every story.\",\n          \"Your voice: grounded, specific, humane; confident-but-comfortable opinionation; concise; educational;\",\n          \"one or two examples per point, never ten; never breathless, never prophetic.\"\n        ],\n        \"laws\": [\n          \"do not impose Koios's historical collapse frame on an event; use systems analysis only when the assignment and admitted sources warrant the particular connection\",\n          \"when a source names a policy, right, framework, or concept without explaining its operational contents, do not invent an explanatory gloss or enumeration for it\",\n          \"do not add temporal priority, causal order, geographic scope, or affected categories that the admitted sources do not state\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"seeds\": [\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"environment\",\n          \"term\": \"climate tipping points\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"environment\",\n          \"term\": \"crop failure and food prices\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"environment\",\n          \"term\": \"urban water scarcity\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"environment\",\n          \"term\": \"insurance climate risk withdrawal\",\n          \"priority\": 9\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"environment\",\n          \"term\": \"extreme heat and infrastructure\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"data center water use\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"AI demand on the grid\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"AI data center power demand\",\n          \"priority\": 9\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"AI infrastructure energy use\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"AI labor displacement\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"AI policy and state capacity\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"semiconductor supply chain fragility\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"satellite internet outage\",\n          \"priority\": 5\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"software security updates\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"technology\",\n          \"term\": \"technology product release dates\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"climate stranded assets\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"AI capital expenditure bubble\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"AI infrastructure debt\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"crypto mining energy demand\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"stablecoin dollar demand\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"crypto liquidity crisis\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"cost of living climate shocks\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"climate disasters and sovereign debt\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"de-dollarization of commodity trade\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"farmland and water rights\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"consumer prices and inflation\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"mortgage and interest rates\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"jobs and unemployment\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"tax deadlines and filing changes\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"economy\",\n          \"term\": \"product recalls and consumer safety\",\n          \"priority\": 7\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"politics\",\n          \"term\": \"climate migration and border policy\",\n          \"priority\": 8\n        },\n        {\n          \"beat\": \"politics\",\n          \"term\": \"AI regulation geopolitics\",\n          \"priority\": 6\n        },\n        {\n  ","contentTruncated":true},{"sourceId":"runtime/lib/law/reported-analysis-genre-contract.json","digest":"sha256:d3f931f03627a8294e4264e0c8350af005d1682d1275946128f8dce01b2876f2","characters":3894,"content":"{\n  \"kind\": \"koios.genre-contract\",\n  \"id\": \"reported-analysis/v1\",\n  \"promise\": \"A timely report organized around one witnessed event, with Koios's systems interpretation visibly subordinate to and licensed by the reporting.\",\n  \"evidenceBudget\": {\n    \"targetWords\": {\n      \"minimum\": 800,\n      \"maximum\": 1100\n    },\n    \"minimumDistinctAssertions\": 15,\n    \"minimumPrimaryAssertions\": 15,\n    \"maximumWordsPerAssertion\": 55,\n    \"law\": \"The requested length is licensed only when the admitted packet carries enough distinct source-bound assertions to sustain it. When the budget does not clear, acquire reporting or commission a narrower genre before writer inference.\"\n  },\n  \"writerPromptLaws\": [\n    \"Write reported analysis, not a thematic essay: the event and the people, institutions, places, dates, quantities, documents, and decisions in the sources remain the article's spine.\",\n    \"Before drafting, silently inventory the packet's supported claims and distinct new details; every paragraph and every section must advance at least one of them rather than restating the frame.\",\n    \"Treat each source as evidence only for its own actors, place, time, scope, attribution, and modality; never use thematic similarity as a bridge between different events.\",\n    \"Koios's systems interpretation may explain a pattern made visible by supported facts, but it may not supply an unreported causal mechanism, motive, consequence, category, or analogy.\",\n    \"Use straight attribution when the source is an allegation, estimate, forecast, interpretation, institutional statement, or contested claim; do not launder it into Koios's voice.\",\n    \"Model output is never evidence. Prefer original and named sources, preserve source motives and uncertainty, and treat consequential claims as publishable only to the extent they are corroborated by the admitted packet.\",\n    \"When the story criticizes a person or institution, alleges wrongdoing, or reports a dispute, represent the subject's response or state only what the admitted reporting establishes about a documented opportunity to respond; otherwise return REPORTING_NEEDED.\",\n    \"Avoid needless harm, sensationalism, stereotypes, unattributed opinion, and commercial influence; keep reported analysis visibly distinct from advocacy and advertising.\",\n    \"A headline may intensify relevance but not certainty; it names the subject before withholding an answer and preserves material attribution, uncertainty, scope, and correction state.\",\n    \"The lede tells the reader what happened, where, to whom, and why it matters now; do not open with a universal thesis, scene-setting abstraction, or generic collapse language.\",\n    \"Do not create a section unless the packet supplies a distinct factual development for it; if fewer than three sections are supportable, refuse with REPORTING_NEEDED instead of padding.\",\n    \"The ending must close on the most consequential supported unresolved fact, decision, deadline, conflict, or question facing the named actors; never substitute an abstract meditation for reporting.\",\n    \"Give readers enough factual payoff in the headline, description, summary, and lede to make an informed click or no-click decision; withhold an answer when useful, never the subject.\"\n  ],\n  \"gates\": [\n    \"event spine\",\n    \"paragraph-level source warrant\",\n    \"attribution and modality preservation\",\n    \"headline-body congruity\",\n    \"non-repetition\",\n    \"correction readiness\",\n    \"exact-manuscript independent editorial acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"derivedFrom\": [\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/journalism.md\",\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md\",\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/circulation-surface.md\",\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md\",\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md\",\n    \"dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md\"\n  ]\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/lib/management/offices/editor-in-chief.json","digest":"sha256:a495154f810510c7e1c32c44a003d6cee817c55bc578bf2272abd836c1fb0de6","characters":654,"content":"{\n  \"kind\": \"koios.office\",\n  \"id\": \"editor-in-chief\",\n  \"incumbent\": \"Nik Koios\",\n  \"authority\": [\n    \"adopt and amend newsroom standards subject to the Leader's mandate\",\n    \"turn audience or public-interest demand into assignments\",\n    \"accept or refuse provider offers for research, reporting, writing, and independent editorial judgment\",\n    \"authorize publication only after exact-manuscript acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"duties\": [\"judging-accountable-publication\", \"learning-from-newsroom-outcomes\"],\n  \"separation\": \"May authorize editorial publication but may not silently grant delivery infrastructure authority or mutate a provider's territory.\"\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/lib/management/duties/judging-accountable-publication.json","digest":"sha256:caf394bee2ed0381b30eeef5250a91279514a70148e3250691ec367c19768be0","characters":964,"content":"{\n  \"kind\": \"koios.duty\",\n  \"id\": \"judging-accountable-publication\",\n  \"office\": \"editor-in-chief\",\n  \"precondition\": \"One exact manuscript, its deterministic standards reading, source and claim records, production provenance, and any prior failure evidence are available.\",\n  \"move\": \"Procure independent judgment from an accepted provider under a provider-validated bounded tool schema, preserve its prose report, and let deterministic Koios code invoke exactly one selected editorial tool. Free-form prose labels never create publication authority.\",\n  \"postcondition\": \"The exact manuscript has an append-only accepted, revise, or refuse judgment carrying the validated tool-selection digest; publication is possible only when submit_editorial_acceptance was selected for deterministically clear bytes.\",\n  \"refusals\": [\"missing source custody\", \"missing provider offer\", \"provider result not accepted\", \"manuscript digest changed\", \"standards gate failed\"]\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/lib/management/duties/learning-from-newsroom-outcomes.json","digest":"sha256:c83849760dd0dd0aa9156bb6eb83234dc48b40c759035dfeebfb452bd38e59e9","characters":873,"content":"{\n  \"kind\": \"koios.duty\",\n  \"id\": \"learning-from-newsroom-outcomes\",\n  \"office\": \"editor-in-chief\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Turn durable newsroom outcomes into bounded replay, routing-review, observation, or standards-review proposals without allowing attention economics to manufacture editorial warrant.\",\n  \"contract\": \"koios-news/newsroom-learning-pulse/v1\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"assignment and newsroom circuit settlements\",\n    \"independent editorial judgments\",\n    \"provider receipts and costs\",\n    \"publication, correction, attention, and revenue observations\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"digest-bound issue readings\",\n    \"typed next-move proposals in the research-lessons ledger\"\n  ],\n  \"mustNot\": [\n    \"publish or replay an issue\",\n    \"silently change a provider route or newsroom standard\",\n    \"treat clicks, revenue, or model availability as evidence for a claim\"\n  ]\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/data/records/research/2026/07/17/2026-07-17-koios-news-research.jsonl","digest":"sha256:e0e4513adc7e7372b8f4bce81bcac2f12ec165c6440a75d9d2230f75c7509261","characters":6059,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"runtime/src/researching/sourcing/source-cycle.mts","digest":"sha256:4ea3f63a61bf03735e924e22753401deb4cc3d14f2123f0d830d8663a5fb0686","characters":15871,"content":"// researching/sourcing/source-cycle ‚Äî one Koios-owned source refresh plus farm\n// tick. This is the operator-visible act that turns external feeds into local\n// wire evidence, then lets the content farm assemble context and draft.\n\nimport { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { dirname, join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport process from \"node:process\";\n\nimport {\n  createContentFarmService,\n  contentFarmCandidateSnapshots,\n  contentFarmCollisionPathSet,\n  contentFarmRepairPacketsReading,\n  contentFarmSourceCyclePlanFromDocument,\n  contentFarmSourceCycleReading,\n  farmCycleReading,\n  normalizeContentFarmCandidateReferences,\n  readContentFarmConfig,\n  readContentFarmConfigDocument,\n  sourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance,\n  sourceCycleDraftInternalLinkSuggestion,\n  restoreContentFarmCandidateWriteCollisions,\n  decodeFrontMatterDocument,\n  encodeFrontMatterDocument,\n  type ContentFarmCandidateState,\n  type FarmCycle,\n  type FarmCycleReading,\n  type ContentFarmRepairPacket,\n  type ContentFarmRepairPacketsReading,\n  type ContentFarmRepairTask,\n  type ContentFarmRepairTaskKind,\n  type ContentFarmSourceCyclePlan,\n  type ContentFarmSourceCycleReading,\n  type ContentFarmSourceCycleWirePlan,\n  type SourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance,\n  type SourceCycleCandidateReferenceNormalization,\n  type SourceCycleCandidateWriteCollision,\n  type ViewCountsReading,\n  type FetchLike,\n} from \"@emsenn/organizing-a-content-farm\";\nimport { createKoiosNewscable } from \"../../cable-app.mjs\";\nimport { DEFAULT_CONTENT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG } from \"../../config.mjs\";\nimport { loadPosts } from \"../../content.mjs\";\nimport { koiosMasthead } from \"../../index.mjs\";\nimport { koiosItems } from \"../../surface.mjs\";\nimport { draftInternalLinkGuidanceReading, type DraftInternalLinkSuggestion } from \"../writing/editing/publishing/managing/circulating/index.mjs\";\nimport { refreshSourceCorpus } from \"./newscable-contract.mjs\";\nimport {\n  KOIOS_DEFAULT_LICENSE,\n  KOIOS_DEFAULT_LICENSE_URL,\n  KOIOS_DEFAULT_SYNDICATION_RIGHTS,\n} from \"../writing/editing/standards.mjs\";\n\nexport type SourceWirePlan = ContentFarmSourceCycleWirePlan;\nexport type KoiosSourceCyclePlan = ContentFarmSourceCyclePlan;\n\nexport type KoiosSourceCycleReading = ContentFarmSourceCycleReading;\n\nexport type KoiosSourceCycleOptions = Readonly<{\n  configPath?: string;\n  fetchImpl?: FetchLike;\n  env?: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>;\n  views?: ViewCountsReading;\n  now?: () => string;\n  onSkip?: (message: string) => void;\n}>;\n\nexport type SourceCycleRepairTaskKind = ContentFarmRepairTaskKind;\nexport type SourceCycleRepairTask = ContentFarmRepairTask;\nexport type SourceCycleCandidateState = ContentFarmCandidateState;\nexport type SourceCycleRepairPacket = ContentFarmRepairPacket;\nexport type SourceCycleRepairPacketsReading = ContentFarmRepairPacketsReading;\n\nasync function contentFarmFetch(\n  configPath: string,\n  upstream: FetchLike,\n  onSkip: (message: string) => void,\n): Promise<FetchLike> {\n  const cable = await createKoiosNewscable(configPath, onSkip);\n  return (async (input: Parameters<FetchLike>[0], init?: Parameters<FetchLike>[1]): Promise<Response> => {\n    const raw = typeof input === \"string\" || input instanceof URL ? String(input) : input.url;\n    const url = new URL(raw);\n    const localCable = (url.hostname === \"127.0.0.1\" || url.hostname === \"localhost\") && url.port === \"18809\";\n    if (!localCable) return upstream(input, init);\n    const surface = await cable.handle(cable.domain, `${url.pathname}${url.search}`);\n    return new Response(surface.body, { status: surface.status, headers: surface.headers });\n  }) as FetchLike;\n}\n\ntype JsonRecord = Record<string, unknown>;\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is JsonRecord {\n  return !!value && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction stringValue(value: unknown, fallback = \"\"): string {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\" ? value.trim() : fallback;\n}\n\nfunction strings(value: unknown): readonly string[] {\n  if (value === undefined || value === null || value === \"\") return Object.freeze([]);\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) return Object.freeze(value.flatMap((item) => strings(item)));\n  return Object.freeze([String(value)]);\n}\n\nfunction manuscriptSlug(frontMatter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>, fallback: string): string {\n  return typeof frontMatter[\"slug\"] === \"string\" && frontMatter[\"slug\"] !== \"\" ? frontMatter[\"slug\"] : fallback;\n}\n\nfunction koiosFrontMatter(frontMatter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>): Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> {\n  const value = frontMatter[\"koios\"];\n  return isRecord(value) ? value : Object.freeze({});\n}\n\nfunction candidateState(contentDir: string | undefined, slug: string): SourceCycleCandidateState {\n  if (contentDir === undefined || slug === \"\") return Object.freeze({ status: \"missing\" as const });\n  const path = join(contentDir, `${slug}.md`);\n  if (!existsSync(path)) return Object.freeze({ status: \"missing\" as const, path });\n  const document = decodeFrontMatterDocument(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"));\n  const title = stringValue(document.frontMatter[\"title\"]);\n  return Object.freeze({\n    status: document.frontMatter[\"draft\"] === true ? \"draft\" as const : \"published\" as const,\n    path,\n    ...(title === \"\" ? {} : { title }),\n  });\n}\n\nexport function sourceCycleRepairPacketsReading(input: Readonly<{\n  runs: readonly unknown[];\n  contentDir?: string;\n  limit?: number;\n}>): SourceCycleRepairPacketsReading {\n  return contentFarmRepairPacketsReading({\n    runs: input.runs,\n    ...(input.limit === undefined ? {} : { limit: input.limit }),\n    candidateState: (slug) => candidateState(input.contentDir, slug),\n    constraints: Object.freeze([\n      \"This is a read-only operator backlog over farm run traces.\",\n      \"Repair packets do not rewrite, publish, or silently normalize manuscripts.\",\n      \"Intake sources remain research material; published citations remain CSL references in manuscript frontmatter and body links.\",\n      \"A published candidate stays visible as historical friction but is not counted as open.\",\n    ]),\n  });\n}\n\nexport function normalizeCandidateReferences(path: string): SourceCycleCandidateReferenceNormalization {\n  const normalized = normalizeContentFarmCandidateReferences({\n    path,\n    license: KOIOS_DEFAULT_LICENSE,\n    licenseUrl: KOIOS_DEFAULT_LICENSE_URL,\n    syndicationRights: KOIOS_DEFAULT_SYNDICATION_RIGHTS,\n  });\n  // Minimal URL promotion cannot know an article title and therefore uses the\n  // host name. Koios's own wire store does know it. Settle that locally before\n  // the reference crosses the publication boundary.\n  const storeRoot = join(dirname(dirname(dirname(resolve(path)))), \"store\");\n  const titles = new Map<string, string>();\n  const walk = (root: string): readonly string[] => {\n    try { return readdirSync(root, { withFileTypes: true }).flatMap((entry) => entry.isDirectory() ? walk(join(root, entry.name)) : entry.name.endsWith(\".json\") ? [join(root, entry.name)] : []); }\n    catch { return []; }\n  };\n  for (const sourcePath of walk(storeRoot)) {\n    try {\n      const bundle = JSON.parse(readFileSync(sourcePath, \"utf8\")) as JsonRecord;\n      const claims = Array.isArray(bundle[\"claims\"]) ? bundle[\"claims\"] : [];\n      let url = \"\"; let title = \"\";\n      for (const claim of claims) {\n        if (!isRecord(claim)) continue;\n        const proposition = isRecord(claim[\"proposition\"]) ? claim[\"proposition\"] : {};\n        if (proposition[\"predicate\"] === \"url\" && typeof proposition[\"object\"] === \"string\") url = proposition[\"object\"];\n        if (proposition[\"predicate\"] === \"title\" && typeof proposition[\"object\"] === \"string\") title = proposition[\"object\"];\n      }\n      if (url !== \"\" && title !== \"\") titles.set(url.replace(/\\/+$/, \"\"), title);\n    } catch { /* malformed wire evidence is ignored by this projection */ }\n  }\n  const document = decodeFrontMatterDocument(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"));\n  const references = Array.isArray(document.frontMatter[\"references\"])\n    ? document.frontMatter[\"references\"].map((reference) => {\n        if (!isRecord(reference)) return reference;\n        const url = typeof reference[\"URL\"] === \"string\" ? reference[\"URL\"].replace(/\\/+$/, \"\") : \"\";\n        const title = titles.get(url);\n        return title === undefined ? reference : Object.freeze({ ...reference, title });\n      })\n    : [];\n  const titleChanged = JSON.stringify(references) !== JSON.stringify(document.frontMatter[\"references\"] ?? []);\n  if (titleChanged) {\n    writeFileSync(path, encodeFrontMatterDocument({\n      kind: \"producing-content.frontmatter-document\" as const,\n      frontMatter: Object.freeze({ ...document.frontMatter, references: Object.freeze(references) }),\n      body: document.body.endsWith(\"\\n\") ? document.body : `${document.body}\\n`,\n    }), \"utf8\");\n  }\n  return Object.freeze({ ...normalized, changed: normalized.changed || titleChanged });\n}\n\nfunction compactDraftLinkSuggestion(suggestion: DraftInternalLinkSuggestion): SourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance[\"suggestions\"][number] {\n  return sourceCycleDraftInternalLinkSuggestion({\n    targetSlug: suggestion.targetSlug,\n    targetPath: suggestion.targetPath,\n    targetHeadline: suggestion.targetHeadline,\n    matchedTerms: suggestion.matchedTerms,\n    confidence: suggestion.confidence,\n    markdownLink: suggestion.markdownLink,\n    writingGuidance: suggestion.writingGuidance,\n  });\n}\n\nexport function enrichCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance(path: string, contentDir = dirname(path)): SourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance {\n  const document = decodeFrontMatterDocument(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\"));\n  const slug = manuscriptSlug(document.frontMatter, path.replace(/^.*\\//, \"\").replace(/\\.md$/, \"\"));\n  const koios = koiosFrontMatter(document.frontMatter);\n  const term = stringValue(koios[\"seo_term\"]) || strings(document.frontMatter[\"keywords\"])[0] || stringValue(document.frontMatter[\"title\"], slug);\n  const beat = stringValue(koios[\"beat\"]);\n  const tags = strings(document.frontMatter[\"tags\"]);\n  const posts = loadPosts(contentDir);\n  const guidance = draftInternalLinkGuidanceReading({\n    posts,\n    items: koiosItems(posts, koiosMasthead()),\n    term,\n    ...(beat === \"\" ? {} : { beat }),\n    tags,\n    excludeSlugs: [slug],\n    limit: 3,\n  });\n  const suggestions = Object.freeze(guidance.suggestions.map(compactDraftLinkSuggestion));\n  const nextKoios = Object.freeze({\n    ...koios,\n    draft_internal_link_guidance: suggestions,\n  });\n  const changed = JSON.stringify(koios[\"draft_internal_link_guidance\"] ?? []) !== JSON.stringify(suggestions);\n  if (changed) {\n    writeFileSync(path, encodeFrontMatterDocument({\n      kind: \"producing-content.frontmatter-document\" as const,\n      frontMatter: Object.freeze({\n        ...document.frontMatter,\n        koios: nextKoios,\n      }),\n      body: document.body.endsWith(\"\\n\") ? document.body : `${document.body}\\n`,\n    }), \"utf8\");\n  }\n  return sourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance({\n    slug,\n    path,\n    changed,\n    suggestions,\n  });\n}\n\nfunction normalizeCycleCandidateReferences(cycle: FarmCycle, collisions: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set()): readonly SourceCycleCandidateReferenceNormalization[] {\n  const normalized: SourceCycleCandidateReferenceNormalization[] = [];\n  for (const reading of cycle.readings) {\n    const run = reading.run;\n    if (run.kind !== \"content.farm.cultivation:witness\" || run.path === null) continue;\n    if (collisions.has(resolve(run.path))) continue;\n    normalized.push(normalizeCandidateReferences(run.path));\n  }\n  return Object.freeze(normalized);\n}\n\nfunction enrichCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinks(cycle: FarmCycle, collisions: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set()): readonly SourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance[] {\n  const enriched: SourceCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance[] = [];\n  for (const reading of cycle.readings) {\n    const run = reading.run;\n    if (run.kind !== \"content.farm.cultivation:witness\" || run.path === null) continue;\n    if (collisions.has(resolve(run.path))) continue;\n    enriched.push(enrichCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance(run.path));\n  }\n  return Object.freeze(enriched);\n}\n\nexport function koiosSourceCyclePlan(options: Pick<KoiosSourceCycleOptions, \"configPath\"> = {}): KoiosSourceCyclePlan {\n  const configPath = options.configPath ?? DEFAULT_CONTENT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG;\n  const document = readContentFarmConfigDocument(configPath);\n  return contentFarmSourceCyclePlanFromDocument({\n    configPath,\n    document,\n    operator: Object.freeze({\n      planUrl: \"https://newsroom.koios.news/operators/source-cycle/plan.json\",\n      runUrl: \"https://newsroom.koios.news/operators/source-cycle\",\n      publicationGate: \"Draft candidates remain draft:true until the editing and publishing offices approve them.\",\n    }),\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function runKoiosSourceCycle(options: KoiosSourceCycleOptions = {}): Promise<KoiosSourceCycleReading> {\n  const configPath = options.configPath ?? DEFAULT_CONTENT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG;\n  const plan = koiosSourceCyclePlan({ configPath });\n  const skippedMessages: string[] = [];\n  const onSkip = (message: string): void => {\n    skippedMessages.push(message);\n    options.onSkip?.(message);\n  };\n  if (options.fetchImpl !== undefined) throw new Error(\"custom in-process fetch cannot cross the separately executable newscable provider boundary; use a declared fixture source instead\");\n  const cableResults = refreshSourceCorpus({ configPath, dataDir: join(dirname(resolve(configPath)), \"data\"), now: (options.now ?? (() => new Date().toISOString()))() }).results;\n  const farmFetch = await contentFarmFetch(configPath, options.fetchImpl ?? fetch, onSkip);\n  const farmConfig = readContentFarmConfig(configPath);\n  const snapshots = contentFarmCandidateSnapshots(farmConfig);\n  const service = createContentFarmService(farmConfig, {\n    fetchImpl: farmFetch,\n    env: options.env ?? process.env,\n    ...(options.views === undefined ? {} : { views: options.views }),\n    ...(options.now === undefined ? {} : { now: options.now }),\n  });\n  const cycle = await service.tick();\n  const candidateWriteCollisions = restoreContentFarmCandidateWriteCollisions(cycle, snapshots, {\n    instruction: \"The farm attempted to write a draft candidate at an existing manuscript path. Koios restored the existing manuscript; create a new assignment or unique draft slug before writing this candidate.\",\n  });\n  const collisionPaths = contentFarmCollisionPathSet(candidateWriteCollisions);\n  const candidateReferences = normalizeCycleCandidateReferences(cycle, collisionPaths);\n  const candidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance = enrichCycleCandidateDraftInternalLinks(cycle, collisionPaths);\n  const farm = farmCycleReading(cycle);\n  return contentFarmSourceCycleReading({\n    generatedAt: (options.now ?? (() => new Date().toISOString()))(),\n    plan,\n    cable: {\n      wireCount: cableResults.length,\n      written: cableResults.reduce((sum, result) => sum + result.written, 0),\n      skipped: cableResults.reduce((sum, result) => sum + result.skipped, 0),\n      errorCount: cableResults.reduce((sum, result) => sum + result.errors.length, 0),\n      results: cableResults,\n      skippedMessages,\n    },\n    farm,\n    candidateWriteCollisions,\n    candidateReferences,\n    candidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance,\n    editorialPolicy: {\n      record: \"draft-candidate\" as const,\n      publication: \"independent-standards-and-editorial-contract\" as const,\n      note: \"The source cycle can write draft candidates and run traces; Koios normalizes candidate citation metadata to CSL references and annotates drafts with same-site link guidance. Publication requires both deterministic standards and an exact-manuscript LISS editorial acceptance, without a per-article human gate.\",\n    },\n  });\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/src/writer-replay.mts","digest":"sha256:3b27ce2b070e82518d70d409bd9b6fe69b0f99ec84b6d2cdf7eabbd0ebc816d6","characters":6849,"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// writer-replay ‚Äî replay one failed Koios cultivation from the Writer layer.\n//\n// This is deliberately narrower than another source cycle: the assignment and\n// reporting packet stay fixed, so a changed outcome measures the Writer and its\n// instructions rather than silently buying different reporting. The previous\n// candidate remains on disk. A same-slug replay receives a revision suffix,\n// and the provider use, exact prompt digest, gates, source URLs, prior\n// manuscript digest, and resulting path are witnessed in Koios-owned data.\n\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { appendFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { basename, dirname, join, resolve } from \"node:path\";\n\nimport {\n  cultivate,\n  decodeFrontMatterDocument,\n  encodeFrontMatterDocument,\n  type CultivationResult,\n} from \"@emsenn/organizing-a-content-farm\";\n\nimport { DEFAULT_CONTENT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG } from \"./config.mjs\";\nimport { koiosFarmProperty } from \"./demand.mjs\";\nimport {\n  enrichCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance,\n  normalizeCandidateReferences,\n} from \"./researching/sourcing/source-cycle.mjs\";\n\ntype JsonRecord = Record<string, unknown>;\n\nconst SITE_ROOT = dirname(DEFAULT_CONTENT_PRODUCTION_CONFIG);\nconst SUBJECT_STORE = join(SITE_ROOT, \"store/decolonization/as-climate-and-conflict-collide-indigenous-leaders-confront-overlapping-crises-at-the-un.json\");\nconst CONTEXT_STORE = join(SITE_ROOT, \"store/decolonization/africa-s-greater-horn-region-is-facing-a-looming-polycrisis-fueled-by-conflict-prices-climate-and-disease.json\");\nconst PRIOR_SLUG = \"indigenous-leaders-confront-the-collision-of-climate-and-conflict\";\nconst TERM = \"extraction and the global south\";\nconst BEAT = \"decolonization\";\n\nfunction isRecord(value: unknown): value is JsonRecord {\n  return !!value && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction claimValue(bundle: JsonRecord, predicate: string): string | undefined {\n  const claims = Array.isArray(bundle[\"claims\"]) ? bundle[\"claims\"] : [];\n  for (const claim of claims) {\n    if (!isRecord(claim)) continue;\n    const proposition = isRecord(claim[\"proposition\"]) ? claim[\"proposition\"] : {};\n    if (proposition[\"predicate\"] !== predicate) continue;\n    const value = proposition[\"object\"];\n    if (typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\") return value.trim();\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\nfunction wireStory(path: string) {\n  const value = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\")) as unknown;\n  if (!isRecord(value)) throw new TypeError(`wire bundle is not an object: ${path}`);\n  const title = claimValue(value, \"title\");\n  const url = claimValue(value, \"url\");\n  if (title === undefined || url === undefined) throw new TypeError(`wire bundle lacks title or URL: ${path}`);\n  return Object.freeze({\n    kind: \"producing-content.syndication-item\" as const,\n    id: typeof value[\"subject\"] === \"string\" ? value[\"subject\"] : basename(path, \".json\"),\n    title,\n    url,\n    ...(claimValue(value, \"summary\") === undefined ? {} : { summary: claimValue(value, \"summary\")! }),\n    ...(claimValue(value, \"published\") === undefined ? {} : { published: claimValue(value, \"published\")! }),\n  });\n}\n\nfunction digest(value: string): string {\n  return `sha256:${createHash(\"sha256\").update(value).digest(\"hex\")}`;\n}\n\nfunction availablePath(contentDir: string, requestedSlug: string): Readonly<{ slug: string; path: string }> {\n  let ordinal = 1;\n  let slug = requestedSlug;\n  let path = join(contentDir, `${slug}.md`);\n  while (existsSync(path)) {\n    ordinal += 1;\n    slug = `${requestedSlug}-revision-${ordinal}`;\n    path = join(contentDir, `${slug}.md`);\n  }\n  return Object.freeze({ slug, path });\n}\n\nfunction replayLogPath(dataDir: string, day: string): string {\n  return join(dataDir, \"records\", \"writer-replays\", day.slice(0, 4), day.slice(5, 7), day.slice(8, 10), `${day}-koios-news-writer-replays.jsonl`);\n}\n\nconst day = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst property = koiosFarmProperty();\nconst subject = wireStory(SUBJECT_STORE);\nconst context = wireStory(CONTEXT_STORE);\nconst priorPath = resolve(property.contentDir, `${PRIOR_SLUG}.md`);\nconst priorBytes = readFileSync(priorPath, \"utf8\");\n\nconst result = await cultivate(property, {\n  at: day,\n  term: TERM,\n  beat: BEAT,\n  items: [subject, context],\n  // Freeze the reporting packet and its roles: this operation is explicitly a\n  // Writer replay, not a second assignment or source-selection decision.\n  select: () => Object.freeze({ story: subject, context: Object.freeze([context]) }),\n  dryRun: true,\n});\n\nif (\"obstruction\" in result) throw new Error(`writer replay obstructed: ${result.evidence}`);\nconst cultivation = result as CultivationResult;\nconst requestedSlug = String(cultivation.document.frontMatter[\"slug\"] ?? cultivation.slug);\nconst destination = availablePath(resolve(property.contentDir), requestedSlug);\nconst document = decodeFrontMatterDocument(encodeFrontMatterDocument(cultivation.document));\nconst nextDocument = Object.freeze({\n  ...document,\n  frontMatter: Object.freeze({\n    ...document.frontMatter,\n    slug: destination.slug,\n    draft: true,\n    koios: Object.freeze({\n      ...(isRecord(document.frontMatter[\"koios\"]) ? document.frontMatter[\"koios\"] : {}),\n      replayed_from: PRIOR_SLUG,\n      replay_layer: \"writer\",\n    }),\n  }),\n});\n\nmkdirSync(dirname(destination.path), { recursive: true });\nwriteFileSync(destination.path, encodeFrontMatterDocument(nextDocument), \"utf8\");\nconst references = normalizeCandidateReferences(destination.path);\nconst internalLinks = enrichCandidateDraftInternalLinkGuidance(destination.path);\nconst finalBytes = readFileSync(destination.path, \"utf8\");\n\nconst record = Object.freeze({\n  kind: \"koios.writer-replay\",\n  at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  replayFrom: \"writer\",\n  assignment: Object.freeze({ term: TERM, beat: BEAT }),\n  sources: Object.freeze([\n    Object.freeze({ role: \"subject\", title: subject.title, url: subject.url }),\n    Object.freeze({ role: \"supporting-context\", title: context.title, url: context.url }),\n  ]),\n  prior: Object.freeze({ slug: PRIOR_SLUG, path: priorPath, digest: digest(priorBytes) }),\n  result: Object.freeze({\n    slug: destination.slug,\n    path: destination.path,\n    digest: digest(finalBytes),\n    shippedByMechanicalGates: cultivation.shipped,\n    gates: cultivation.gates,\n    usage: cultivation.usage,\n    inference: Object.freeze({ provider: property.provider ?? \"nim\", model: property.model ?? \"provider-default\" }),\n    composition: cultivation.composition,\n    references,\n    internalLinks,\n  }),\n});\nconst logPath = replayLogPath(resolve(property.dataDir), day);\nmkdirSync(dirname(logPath), { recursive: true });\nappendFileSync(logPath, `${JSON.stringify(record)}\\n`, \"utf8\");\n\nprocess.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`);\n"},{"sourceId":"runtime/src/newsroom/departments.mts","digest":"sha256:3bc17f1e61592b3759150160a274078ccf5cb272c11f0656dcd99addfd6b487d","characters":3045,"content":"// newsroom/departments ‚Äî the whole Koios.News production line as one reading.\n\nimport type { KoiosPost } from \"../content.mjs\";\nimport type { SearchConsoleQuery } from \"../demand.mjs\";\nimport { administratingOfficeReading, type AdministratingOfficeReading } from \"../administrating/index.mjs\";\nimport { researchDepartmentReading, type ResearchDepartmentReading } from \"../researching/index.mjs\";\nimport { writingDepartmentReading, type WritingDepartmentReading } from \"../researching/writing/index.mjs\";\nimport { editingDepartmentReading, type EditingDepartmentReading } from \"../researching/writing/editing/index.mjs\";\nimport { publishingDepartmentReading, type PublishingDepartmentReading } from \"../researching/writing/editing/publishing/index.mjs\";\nimport { koiosItems, type KoiosItem, type KoiosMasthead } from \"../surface.mjs\";\nimport { desksReading, type DesksReading } from \"../researching/sourcing/desks.mjs\";\nimport type { ViewCounts } from \"../views.mjs\";\n\nexport type KoiosNewsroomDepartments = Readonly<{\n  kind: \"koios.newsroom.departments\";\n  // The two orthogonal axes of the newsroom: desks are topical standing (what\n  // we cover), departments are the production line (how a desk's stories are\n  // made). Every story crosses every department and belongs to one desk.\n  desks: DesksReading;\n  administrating: AdministratingOfficeReading;\n  researching: ResearchDepartmentReading & Readonly<{\n    writing: WritingDepartmentReading & Readonly<{\n      editing: EditingDepartmentReading & Readonly<{\n        publishing: PublishingDepartmentReading;\n      }>;\n    }>;\n  }>;\n}>;\n\nexport function newsroomDepartmentsReading(input: Readonly<{\n  posts: readonly KoiosPost[];\n  masthead: KoiosMasthead;\n  views: ViewCounts;\n  dataDir: string;\n  adClient?: string;\n  searchConsole?: readonly SearchConsoleQuery[];\n}>): KoiosNewsroomDepartments {\n  const items: readonly KoiosItem[] = koiosItems(input.posts, input.masthead);\n  const researching = researchDepartmentReading({\n    posts: input.posts,\n    views: input.views,\n    dataDir: input.dataDir,\n    ...(input.searchConsole === undefined ? {} : { searchConsole: input.searchConsole }),\n  });\n  const writing = writingDepartmentReading(input.posts);\n  const editing = editingDepartmentReading(input.posts);\n  const publishing = publishingDepartmentReading({\n    masthead: input.masthead,\n    items,\n    posts: input.posts,\n    views: input.views,\n    dataDir: input.dataDir,\n    ...(input.adClient === undefined ? {} : { adClient: input.adClient }),\n  });\n  return Object.freeze({\n    kind: \"koios.newsroom.departments\",\n    desks: desksReading({ articles: items.map((item) => ({ section: item.section, published: item.published, isPublic: item.isPublic })) }),\n    administrating: administratingOfficeReading({ adSenseEnabled: input.adClient !== undefined }),\n    researching: Object.freeze({\n      ...researching,\n      writing: Object.freeze({\n        ...writing,\n        editing: Object.freeze({\n          ...editing,\n          publishing,\n        }),\n      }),\n    }),\n  });\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"prior-art/agentic-newsroom","digest":"sha256:ea72ce19c111400ed98fe56670cccd7dfbb64fe7c58ecbf5a228e65ce75115f5","characters":41505,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"prior-art/news-topology","digest":"sha256:cfdc0e5d3b5fa55fbcdc30f77d49a6bbff82010c27087de76d6e89ca9c364b88","characters":51589,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"prior-art/claims-to-prose","digest":"sha256:2102054762017657d5996820d1e5ca4d41eb46a6d28cdb0ea1721a7ade343a2b","characters":50052,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"prior-art/accountable-attention","digest":"sha256:4b0ab52501d6ae3734b2266102cd9d015b14aba70f89c3b0fc26ab7793945503","characters":38791,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/researching-skill","digest":"sha256:c7b8b08da65b85ac04722940e6e7b29c161bdd1a2a5cb0dd5652bac874d9cfcd","characters":3320,"content":"---\nname: researching\ndescription: Find the day's story ‚Äî an under-discussed current event that is a window onto collapse ‚Äî and fix its single SEO term. Run this first; its brief feeds writing.\n---\n\n# Researching a Koios.News story\n\nThe job is not to cover the biggest headline.\nIt is to find the event that is **under-discussed relative to how much it reveals** ‚Äî the small fracture that is a clear window onto the larger emergent phenomenon.\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Scan the last 24 hours to 7 days** of news.\n  Only use events you can confirm happened within the last week.\n2. **Pick for revelation, not size.** Favour an event that (a) is not being widely discussed, and (b) connects cleanly to the collapse frame ‚Äî climate breakdown as upstream cause, a compounding feedback rather than an isolated incident.\n3. **Find the primary sources.** Get title, author, and permalink for each.\n  You will cite these, not paraphrase them away.\n4. **Name the synthetic frame** ‚Äî the one sentence that says what larger system this event is a window onto.\n5. **Choose the single SEO term.** One term the whole post will align to; it must read naturally in a first paragraph and in a subheader.\n6. **Feasibility-check** any future the event implies: can the world actually support that adaptation at that point?\n\n## Output: a research brief\n\nWrite a brief to `library/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` (use the script).\nIt carries: the event, the confirmed primary sources, why it is under-discussed, the chosen SEO term, and the collapse-connection angle.\nThe brief is what `working/writing/` consumes.\n\n## Working from a specific source\n\nSometimes the story starts the other way round: someone hands you ONE source ‚Äî a think-tank dispatch, an investigation, a report ‚Äî and asks whether it belongs in Koios.\nThe **submission desk** is for that.\nIt does not paraphrase the source into a post; it appraises beat fit, then *finds more* ‚Äî pulling related items out of the beat's own wires (and any sources you already found by hand) ‚Äî and synthesizes original, multi-source analysis anchored on the seed, through the same cultivation cycle every article runs through.\n\n- A source outside every Koios beat is witnessed as out-of-frame and never drafted (the same lawful shape as unsupported demand).\n- The seed leads; related wire matches and your discoveries are the supporting context the analysis draws on.\n  Aim for several real sources cited, not one.\n- The draft candidate is a starting point, not the post.\n  A single-source LLM rewrite is slop; the editor's job is the original synthesis across the gathered sources, with every figure and claim warranted.\n\n```sh\n# JSON on stdin (url + title required; summary/text/beat/term optional):\necho '{\"url\":\"‚Ä¶\",\"title\":\"‚Ä¶\",\"summary\":\"‚Ä¶\",\"beat\":\"collapse-conflict\"}' \\\n  | pnpm --filter @emsenn/koios.news run source:submit\n```\n\nIn code, `submitSource(seed, { mode: \"expand\", discoveredSources })` from `@emsenn/koios.news/researching/sourcing`; `gatherRelatedSources(...)\n` exposes the \"find more\" step on its own.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `scripts/new-brief.mjs \"<title>\" <seo-term>` ‚Äî scaffold a dated brief in `library/` with the sections above, ready to fill in.\n- `pnpm --filter @emsenn/koios.news run source:submit` ‚Äî submit one specific source (JSON on stdin) for appraisal and multi-source expansion.\n"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/researching-script","digest":"sha256:fcc86113bbe2b0af9518e8c62bb5ab4ed83e388cbca5388972dd50ae15d6c1ca","characters":1518,"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// new-brief.mjs ‚Äî scaffold a dated Koios.News research brief.\n// Usage: node new-brief.mjs \"<title>\" \"<seo term>\"\n// Writes working/researching/library/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md (won't overwrite).\n\nimport { writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { dirname, resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst [, , title, seoTerm] = process.argv;\nif (!title) {\n  console.error('usage: new-brief.mjs \"<title>\" \"<seo term>\"');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nconst here = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst library = resolve(here, \"..\", \"library\");\nconst today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst slug = title\n  .toLowerCase()\n  .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, \"-\")\n  .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, \"\");\nconst file = resolve(library, `${today}-${slug}.md`);\n\nif (existsSync(file)) {\n  console.error(`refusing to overwrite ${file}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nconst brief = `---\ntitle: \"${title}\"\ndate: ${today}\nseo_term: \"${seoTerm ?? \"\"}\"\nstatus: brief\n---\n\n# ${title}\n\n## The event\n<!-- what happened, confirmed within the last 7 days -->\n\n## Primary sources\n<!-- title ‚Äî author ‚Äî permalink, one per line -->\n-\n\n## Why it is under-discussed\n<!-- what the coverage is missing -->\n\n## The collapse-connection angle\n<!-- one sentence: what larger system this is a window onto -->\n\n## Feasibility check\n<!-- can the world support the future this implies, at that point? -->\n`;\n\nmkdirSync(library, { recursive: true });\nwriteFileSync(file, brief);\nconsole.log(file);\n"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/writing-skill","digest":"sha256:11d1256363331bd77cd07ddba00f384285b16ba931849d97a9709d724dd61968","characters":1950,"content":"---\nname: writing\ndescription: Draft a Koios.News post from a research brief ‚Äî the article plus its excerpt, meta description, and tweet ‚Äî in the site's frontmatter shape. Consumes a researching brief; hands off to editing.\n---\n\n# Writing a Koios.News post\n\nTake a brief from `working/researching/library/` and turn it into a publishable draft in `content/posts/`.\nWrite in Nik's voice (see `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Shape of the article\n\n- **Lede (first paragraph):** state the event plainly and land the **SEO term** in it.\n  Then the turn ‚Äî why this is a fracture, not an incident.\n- **Subheaders (`##`):** the SEO term appears in at least one.\n  Each section reads the event through the collapse frame; no section treats it as isolated.\n- **Length:** ‚â• 800 words.\n- **Citations:** primary sources by title, author, permalink ‚Äî linked inline.\n  Never paraphrase a source's argument away.\n- **Close:** tie the event into the larger compounding pattern.\n  A vision, never a prophecy ‚Äî \"might\", not \"will\".\n\n## The three extra outputs (frontmatter, not body)\n\nEvery post also carries, in its frontmatter ‚Äî never as trailing sections in the body:\n\n- `summary` ‚Äî a ~50-word excerpt, SEO term included.\n- `description` ‚Äî a ~120-character meta description for link previews.\n- `koios.tweet` ‚Äî one share sentence with an emoji, no hashtags, SEO term included.\n\n## Frontmatter shape\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"...\"            # the descriptive headline\ndate: YYYY-MM-DD\ndraft: true             # editing clears this when the post ships\nauthor: \"Nik Koios\"\nslug: \"...\"\ndescription: \"...\"      # ~120 char meta\nsummary: \"...\"         # ~50 word excerpt\nkeywords: [\"<seo term>\"]\ncategories: [\"Climate Breakdown\"]\ntags: [\"...\", \"...\"]\nkoios:\n  seo_term: \"<seo term>\"\n  tweet: \"...\"\n```\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `scripts/new-post.mjs \"<title>\" <seo-term>` ‚Äî scaffold the post file in `content/posts/<slug>.md` with this frontmatter and section stubs, dated today and marked `draft: true`.\n"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/writing-script","digest":"sha256:a9401614ae752bd90babd5e79fac95a5cda08aafa580cb2f9ced697590d0b709","characters":1641,"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// new-post.mjs ‚Äî scaffold a Koios.News post in the site's frontmatter shape.\n// Usage: node new-post.mjs \"<title>\" \"<seo term>\"\n// Writes content/posts/<slug>.md (won't overwrite), marked draft: true.\n\nimport { writeFileSync, existsSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { dirname, resolve } from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst [, , title, seoTerm] = process.argv;\nif (!title) {\n  console.error('usage: new-post.mjs \"<title>\" \"<seo term>\"');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nconst here = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n// here = working/writing/scripts -> up 3 to package root, then into content.\nconst posts = resolve(here, \"..\", \"..\", \"..\", \"content\", \"posts\");\nconst today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst slug = title\n  .toLowerCase()\n  .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, \"-\")\n  .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, \"\");\nconst file = resolve(posts, `${slug}.md`);\nconst term = seoTerm ?? \"\";\n\nif (existsSync(file)) {\n  console.error(`refusing to overwrite ${file}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nconst post = `---\ntitle: \"${title}\"\ndate: ${today}\ndraft: true\nauthor: \"Nik Koios\"\nslug: \"${slug}\"\ndescription: \"\"\nsummary: \"\"\nkeywords: [\"${term}\"]\ncategories: [\"Climate Breakdown\"]\ntags: []\nkoios:\n  seo_term: \"${term}\"\n  tweet: \"\"\n---\n\n<!-- Lede: state the event and land \"${term}\" here. Then the turn. -->\n\n## <!-- a subheader; \"${term}\" should appear in at least one -->\n\n<!-- read the event through the collapse frame; cite primary sources inline -->\n\n## What this is a window onto\n\n<!-- tie it into the larger compounding pattern ‚Äî a vision, never a prophecy -->\n`;\n\nwriteFileSync(file, post);\nconsole.log(file);\n"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/editing-skill","digest":"sha256:25461a6e6e0dd3346eff46bbd902caa87c2e93b79f866b7f71b2080c08a609b6","characters":1525,"content":"---\nname: editing\ndescription: Audit a draft before it ships ‚Äî voice, SEO-term placement, citations, length, and the no-prophecy rule. Mostly mechanical checks via lint-post; the judgment calls are voice and citations.\n---\n\n# Editing a Koios.News post\n\nNothing ships until it passes here.\nTwo layers: the mechanical checks (run the linter) and the judgment checks (you, reading as Nik).\n\n## Mechanical ‚Äî run the linter\n\n`scripts/lint-post.mjs content/posts/<slug>.md` checks:\n\n- body length ‚â• 800 words;\n- the SEO term (`koios.seo_term`) appears in the **first paragraph**;\n- the SEO term appears in **at least one `##` subheader**;\n- `summary` (~50 words), `description` (~120 chars), and `koios.tweet` are all present and non-empty;\n- reports the `draft` state.\n\nIt exits non-zero if a hard check fails.\nFix and re-run until clean.\n\n## Judgment ‚Äî read it as Nik\n\n- **Voice.** Confident-but-comfortable, content-farm register, concise.\n  No hedging filler, no academic throat-clearing.\n  One or two examples, not a pile.\n- **Citations.** Every claim that needs a source has one, by title/author/ permalink, linked inline.\n  No source's argument paraphrased away.\n- **No prophecy.** Scan for \"will happen\" / certainty about the future.\n  A vision is \"might\", not \"will\".\n  Rewrite anything that predicts.\n- **Not isolated.** Every section connects the event to the larger compounding phenomenon.\n  Cut any paragraph that treats it as a one-off.\n\n## Scripts\n\n- `scripts/lint-post.mjs <post.md>` ‚Äî the mechanical checks above.\n"},{"sourceId":"newsroom/editing-script","digest":"sha256:da7ce1fe61d2ebf288bca6595073cc747ae4137503892a89c7357ed8d181a8db","characters":2542,"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// lint-post.mjs ‚Äî mechanical pre-publish checks for a Koios.News post.\n// Usage: node lint-post.mjs <path/to/post.md>\n// Exit 0 if all hard checks pass, 1 otherwise. Soft checks print warnings.\n\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst path = process.argv[2];\nif (!path) {\n  console.error(\"usage: lint-post.mjs <post.md>\");\n  process.exit(2);\n}\n\nconst raw = readFileSync(path, \"utf8\");\nconst m = raw.match(/^---\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\n---\\n([\\s\\S]*)$/);\nif (!m) {\n  console.error(\"‚úó no YAML frontmatter found\");\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nconst [, fm, body] = m;\n\n// --- tiny frontmatter field readers (good enough for our flat + koios shape) ---\nconst top = (k) => {\n  const r = fm.match(new RegExp(`^${k}:\\\\s*\"?(.*?)\"?\\\\s*$`, \"m\"));\n  return r ? r[1] : null;\n};\nconst koios = (k) => {\n  const r = fm.match(new RegExp(`^\\\\s{2,}${k}:\\\\s*\"?(.*?)\"?\\\\s*$`, \"m\"));\n  return r ? r[1] : null;\n};\n\nconst seoTerm = koios(\"seo_term\") || (top(\"keywords\") || \"\").replace(/[[\\]\"]/g, \"\");\nconst summary = top(\"summary\");\nconst description = top(\"description\");\nconst tweet = koios(\"tweet\");\nconst draft = top(\"draft\");\n\nconst words = body.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;\nconst firstPara = body.trim().split(/\\n\\s*\\n/)[0] || \"\";\nconst subheads = [...body.matchAll(/^##\\s+(.*)$/gm)].map((x) => x[1]);\nconst has = (hay, needle) =>\n  needle && hay.toLowerCase().includes(needle.toLowerCase());\n\nconst fails = [];\nconst warns = [];\n\nif (!seoTerm) fails.push(\"no seo_term / keywords set\");\nif (words < 800) fails.push(`body is ${words} words (need ‚â• 800)`);\nif (seoTerm && !has(firstPara, seoTerm))\n  fails.push(`SEO term \"${seoTerm}\" not in the first paragraph`);\nif (seoTerm && !subheads.some((h) => has(h, seoTerm)))\n  fails.push(`SEO term \"${seoTerm}\" not in any ## subheader`);\nif (!summary) fails.push(\"summary (excerpt) is empty\");\nif (!description) fails.push(\"description (meta) is empty\");\nif (!tweet) fails.push(\"koios.tweet is empty\");\n\nif (summary) {\n  const sw = summary.split(/\\s+/).length;\n  if (sw < 35 || sw > 65) warns.push(`summary is ${sw} words (aim ~50)`);\n}\nif (description && description.length > 160)\n  warns.push(`description is ${description.length} chars (aim ~120)`);\nif (draft === \"true\") warns.push(\"draft: true ‚Äî not yet publishable\");\n\nconst name = path.split(\"/\").pop();\nfor (const w of warns) console.log(`  ‚ö† ${name}: ${w}`);\nfor (const f of fails) console.log(`  ‚úó ${name}: ${f}`);\nif (fails.length === 0) console.log(`  ‚úì ${name}: ${words} words, checks pass`);\n\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\n"},{"sourceId":"production/cultivate","digest":"sha256:3d42f91acecc741406650acacd256f315404079171ddb06cdb2c49bebcb87b31","characters":28349,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"production/newsroom","digest":"sha256:82ee425e74ce304788d860ec27b3d9fca7803e61fc42d29028b27c7e953ec0a2","characters":18275,"content":"/**\n * newsroom ‚Äî the NEWSROOM FIBER over the content-farm cycle.\n *\n * Per emsenn (2026-06-15): \"newsroom is meant to be a specialization of\n * content-farm, where its special functions are parameters into a content-farm.\"\n * This module harvests those special functions out of the (retiring) standalone\n * `@emsenn/newsroom` package and exposes them as content-farm SEAM parameters ‚Äî\n * `select`/`compose`/`record` ‚Äî so a newsroom is literally\n * `cultivate(property, { ...options, ...newsroomProfile })`, not a parallel\n * engine. See dev/docs/notes/2026-06-15-newsroom-as-fiber-over-content-farm.md.\n *\n * This file currently carries the COMPOSE seam (multi-paper brief synthesis,\n * the newsroom reporter's voice); the SELECT seam (angle clustering) and the\n * RECORD seam (claim-state assertion trace) fold in next. The synthesis\n * functions are kept exported in their own right ‚Äî they are real capabilities\n * (grounded multi-source briefing) and must not be lost.\n */\n\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\n\nimport type { SyndicationItem, FetchLike, SyndicationAdapter } from \"../syndication/index.mjs\";\nimport type { PostDraft, FarmGate } from \"../topology/article.mjs\";\nimport {\n  write, clearGate, assertionsFromWrites, claimSetsFromTrace, newsSlug,\n  type NewsClaimWrite, type NewsAssertionTrace, type NewsClaimSet,\n} from \"../topology/news/index.mjs\";\nimport { cultivate, intakeItems } from \"./cultivate.mjs\";\nimport type { Ask, ComposeDraft, SelectStory, RecordCycle, CycleSettlement, CultivationObstruction } from \"./cultivate.mjs\";\nimport type { DemandEntry } from \"./demand.mjs\";\nimport type { FarmProperty } from \"./property.mjs\";\n\nconst unique = <T,>(xs: readonly T[]): T[] => [...new Set(xs)];\n\n// ---------- prose normalization (harvested from @emsenn/newsroom) ----------\n\n/** Strip the tics an LLM leaves in a brief: bold runs, \"headline:\"/\"report:\"\n * prefixes, empty `(Source: )` stubs, bare citation brackets, and the spacing\n * those removals leave behind. */\nexport function cleanProse(value: unknown): string {\n  return String(value ?? \"\")\n    .replace(/\\*\\*([^*]+)\\*\\*/g, \"$1\")\n    .replace(/^\\s*(?:headline|report):\\s*/i, \"\")\n    .replace(/\\s*\\(Source:\\s*\\)\\.?/gi, \".\")\n    .replace(/\\[[\\d,\\s]+\\]/g, \" \")\n    .replace(/\\s+([.!?,;:])/g, \"$1\")\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n    .trim();\n}\n\n/** Split a reply into clean, single-idea sentences; blanks are dropped. */\nexport function sentences(value: unknown): readonly string[] {\n  const text = cleanProse(value);\n  if (!text) return Object.freeze([]);\n  return Object.freeze(text.split(/(?<=[.!?])\\s+/).map(cleanProse).filter((line) => line.length > 1));\n}\n\n// ---------- brief synthesis (harvested from @emsenn/newsroom) ----------\n\n/** A reporter's brief: one headline sentence and the coverage findings. The\n * claim-state-first shape ‚Äî prose is a lossy projection of these. */\nexport type StructuredBrief = Readonly<{ headline: string; findings: readonly string[] }>;\n\n/** The reporter prompt: ground a short brief ONLY in the bundled sources. */\nexport function synthesisPrompt(systemPrompt: string, topic: string, papers: readonly SyndicationItem[]): string {\n  const bundle = papers.map((paper, index) => `[${index + 1}] ${paper.title}: ${paper.summary ?? \"\"}`).join(\"\\n\\n\");\n  return `${systemPrompt}\\n\\nTopic: \"${topic}\". Sources:\\n\\n${bundle}\\n\\n` +\n    \"Write a short news brief grounded only in the sources above: one headline sentence, then 3 to 6 short, single-idea sentences of coverage.\";\n}\n\n/** Read a reply into a brief: the first sentence is the headline, the rest are\n * findings. A reply with no prose is an error ‚Äî synthesis produced nothing. */\nexport function structureBrief(reply: unknown): StructuredBrief {\n  const parts = sentences(reply);\n  if (parts.length === 0) throw new Error(\"synthesis returned no prose\");\n  return Object.freeze({ headline: parts[0]!, findings: Object.freeze(parts.slice(1)) });\n}\n\n/** Synthesize a brief over the bundled papers through the injected `ask`. */\nexport async function synthesizeBrief(\n  ask: Ask,\n  params: Readonly<{ systemPrompt?: string; topic: string; papers: readonly SyndicationItem[] }>,\n): Promise<StructuredBrief> {\n  return structureBrief(await ask(synthesisPrompt(params.systemPrompt ?? \"\", params.topic, params.papers)));\n}\n\n// ---------- the newsroom COMPOSE seam ----------\n\n/** The newsroom's composition: synthesize a brief over the selected story and\n * its context (the cycle's intake = the reporter's papers), grounding every\n * claim in those sources, and project the brief into a PostDraft. Unlike the\n * farm default (one freeform draft prompt), the newsroom reporter writes a\n * source-bounded brief ‚Äî headline + single-idea findings. */\nexport const newsroomCompose: ComposeDraft = async ({ voice, term, story, context, ask }) => {\n  const papers = [story, ...context];\n  const systemPrompt = [...voice.persona, ...(voice.laws ?? [])].join(\" \");\n  const brief = await synthesizeBrief(ask, { systemPrompt, topic: term, papers });\n  const body = brief.findings.join(\"\\n\\n\");\n  const draft: PostDraft = {\n    kind: \"producing-content.article.draft\" as const,\n    title: brief.headline,\n    description: brief.headline,\n    summary: brief.findings[0] ?? brief.headline,\n    tweet: brief.headline,\n    tags: [],\n    body: body.length > 0 ? body : brief.headline,\n  };\n  return Object.freeze({ draft, copyedits: [] });\n};\n\n// ---------- angle clustering (harvested from @emsenn/newsroom) ----------\n\nconst STOP_WORDS = new Set((\"the a an of to in on for and or with from is are be been by as at into over under \" +\n  \"new using based via this that these those their its it can will more most toward across within news agent agents web\").split(\" \"));\n\n/** The content words of a string (4+ letters, stop-words removed, de-duped) ‚Äî\n * the basis for keyword-overlap clustering. */\nexport function keywordsOf(value: unknown): readonly string[] {\n  return unique((String(value ?? \"\").toLowerCase().match(/[a-z]{4,}/g) ?? []).filter((word) => !STOP_WORDS.has(word)));\n}\n\n/** The assignment-editor prompt: from today's intake, name the N strongest\n * distinct story angles worth assigning. */\nexport function assignmentPrompt(voice: string, topic: string, articles: readonly SyndicationItem[], max = 3): string {\n  const publication = articles.map((article, index) => `${index + 1}. ${article.title}`).join(\"\\n\");\n  return `${voice.replace(/\\{topic\\}/g, topic)}\\n\\nHere is today's source intake. Name the ${max} strongest distinct story angles worth assigning, one per line.\\n\\nSource observations:\\n${publication}`;\n}\n\n/** Read the assignment editor's reply into clean angle lines, dropping\n * preamble, empty headers, and numbering. */\nexport function parseAngles(reply: unknown): readonly string[] {\n  return Object.freeze(String(reply ?? \"\").split(\"\\n\")\n    .map((line) => cleanProse(line.replace(/^[\\s>*\\-\\d.)]+/, \"\")))\n    .filter((line) => line.length > 4 && /[a-z]/i.test(line))\n    .filter((line) => !/:\\s*$/.test(line))\n    .filter((line) => !/^(here are|the following|below are|these are|sure|certainly|okay|here's)\\b/i.test(line)));\n}\n\n/** Cluster the intake by keyword overlap with an angle, returning the matching\n * source subjects in descending relevance (the newsroom's source-clustering\n * capability; used by the angle-assignment layer). */\nexport function clusterSources(angle: string, articles: readonly SyndicationItem[], sourceSubjects: readonly string[], max = 5): readonly string[] {\n  const angleKeywords = keywordsOf(angle);\n  return Object.freeze(articles\n    .map((article, index) => ({\n      source: sourceSubjects[index],\n      score: keywordsOf(article.title).filter((word) => angleKeywords.includes(word)).length,\n    }))\n    .filter((candidate): candidate is { source: string; score: number } => candidate.score > 0 && !!candidate.source)\n    .sort((left, right) => right.score - left.score)\n    .slice(0, max)\n    .map((candidate) => candidate.source));\n}\n\n// ---------- the newsroom SELECT seam ----------\n\n/** The newsroom's selection: the assigned term IS the angle. Rather than the\n * farm's term-as-lens single-story pick, the newsroom clusters the intake by\n * keyword overlap with the angle ‚Äî the best-matching item leads, the rest of\n * the cluster is the reporter's context (the papers the brief is grounded in).\n * With no keyword match it falls back to the intake order, so the cycle always\n * settles on a story. */\nexport const newsroomSelect: SelectStory = ({ term, items }) => {\n  const angleKeywords = keywordsOf(term);\n  const scored = items\n    .map((item) => ({ item, score: keywordsOf(`${item.title} ${item.summary ?? \"\"}`).filter((word) => angleKeywords.includes(word)).length }))\n    .sort((left, right) => right.score - left.score);\n  const matched = scored.filter((entry) => entry.score > 0);\n  const ranked = matched.length > 0 ? matched : scored;\n  const story = ranked[0]?.item ?? items[0]!;\n  const context = ranked.slice(1, 6).map((entry) => entry.item);\n  return { story, context };\n};\n\n// ---------- claim-state writes (harvested from @emsenn/newsroom) ----------\n\n/** The subject atom for a source observation: prefix + the article's id (arXiv\n * abs ids stripped to their bare form), or its url/title. */\nexport function articleSubject(prefix: string, article: Pick<SyndicationItem, \"id\" | \"url\" | \"title\">): string {\n  const rawId = article.id ?? article.url ?? article.title;\n  const arxivId = typeof article.id === \"string\" ? article.id.replace(/^https?:\\/\\/arxiv\\.org\\/abs\\//, \"\") : rawId;\n  return newsSlug(`${prefix} ${arxivId}`);\n}\n\n/** The source observation as a claim write: title and url, plus abstract,\n * publication date, authors, and categories when present. */\nexport function sourceWrites(article: SyndicationItem, opts: Readonly<{ prefix?: string; citation?: string }> = {}): readonly NewsClaimWrite[] {\n  const prefix = opts.prefix ?? article.source ?? \"source\";\n  const subject = articleSubject(prefix, article);\n  const citation = opts.citation ?? article.url;\n  const claims: Record<string, unknown> = { title: article.title, url: article.url };\n  if (article.summary) claims[\"abstract\"] = article.summary;\n  if (article.published) claims[\"published\"] = article.published;\n  if (article.authors && article.authors.length > 0) claims[\"author\"] = [...article.authors];\n  if (article.categories && article.categories.length > 0) claims[\"category\"] = [...article.categories];\n  return Object.freeze([write(subject, claims, citation)]);\n}\n\n/** A brief as claim writes: the headline cell and (when present) the findings\n * cell, both cited to the reporter. */\nexport function briefWrites(subject: string, brief: StructuredBrief, citation = \"newsroom:reporter\"): readonly NewsClaimWrite[] {\n  const writes: NewsClaimWrite[] = [write(subject, { headline: brief.headline }, citation)];\n  if (brief.findings.length > 0) writes.push(write(subject, { finds: [...brief.findings] }, citation));\n  return Object.freeze(writes);\n}\n\n// ---------- the newsroom RECORD seam ----------\n\n/** The newsroom's witness: instead of a markdown candidate, the cycle's\n * settlement is carried out as a claim-state ASSERTION TRACE (the canonical\n * carrier ‚Äî every source observation, the angle and its draws-on links, the\n * brief, and each editorial gate, charged) and the CLAIM SETS folded back out\n * of it. Per the news-topology theory the trace is canonical and prose is the\n * lossy projection. */\nexport type NewsroomCultivation = Readonly<{\n  kind: \"content.farm.newsroom-cultivation:witness\";\n  property: string;\n  assignment: DemandEntry;\n  story: SyndicationItem;\n  draft: PostDraft;\n  gates: readonly FarmGate[];\n  shipped: boolean;\n  assertionTrace: NewsAssertionTrace;\n  claimSets: readonly NewsClaimSet[];\n  path: string | null;\n  usage: Readonly<{ calls: number; tokens: number }>;\n  intakeObstructions: readonly string[];\n}>;\n\n/** The newsroom's recording: fold the settlement into claim writes ‚Äî source\n * observations for the story and its context, the angle and its draws-on\n * links, the brief, the editorial gates (a failed gate is a denial), and the\n * published status when shipped ‚Äî assert them into a trace, and fold the trace\n * back into per-subject claim sets. Persists the trace + claim sets as JSON\n * under the property's data dir unless dry-run. */\nexport const newsroomRecord: RecordCycle<NewsroomCultivation> = (settlement: CycleSettlement, ctx) => {\n  const { property, assignment, story, context, draft, gates, shipped, usage, intakeObstructions } = settlement;\n  const papers = [story, ...context];\n  const subject = newsSlug(draft.title).split(\"-\").slice(0, 9).join(\"-\") || `${property.name}-${ctx.at}`;\n  const citation = `newsroom:${property.name}`;\n  const sourceSubjects = unique(papers.map((item) => articleSubject(item.source ?? \"source\", item)));\n  const findings = sentences(draft.body);\n  const writes: NewsClaimWrite[] = [\n    ...papers.flatMap((item) => sourceWrites(item, { prefix: item.source ?? \"source\" })),\n    write(subject, { angle: assignment.term, \"draws-on\": sourceSubjects }, citation),\n    ...briefWrites(subject, { headline: draft.title, findings }, citation),\n    ...gates.map((gate) => clearGate(subject, gate.gate, gate.charge === \"pass\", `desk:${gate.gate}`)),\n    ...(shipped ? [write(subject, { status: \"published\", \"published-at\": ctx.at }, citation)] : []),\n  ];\n  const assertionTrace = assertionsFromWrites(writes, { transaction: ctx.at });\n  const claimSets = claimSetsFromTrace(assertionTrace);\n  let path: string | null = null;\n  if (!ctx.dryRun) {\n    const dir = join(property.dataDir, \"newsroom\");\n    mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n    path = join(dir, `${subject}.json`);\n    writeFileSync(path, `${JSON.stringify({ subject, shipped, assertionTrace, claimSets })}\\n`, \"utf8\");\n  }\n  return Object.freeze({\n    kind: \"content.farm.newsroom-cultivation:witness\" as const,\n    property: property.name,\n    assignment,\n    story,\n    draft,\n    gates,\n    shipped,\n    assertionTrace,\n    claimSets,\n    path,\n    usage,\n    intakeObstructions,\n  });\n};\n\n// ---------- the newsroom CYCLE (the N-angles-per-run orchestration) ----------\n\n/** Ask the assignment editor for the strongest distinct angles in today's\n * intake. The assignment is the OUTER layer of the newsroom fiber: it chooses\n * WHICH angles to run; the per-angle cultivation (selection ‚Üí composition ‚Üí\n * recording) is one base cycle each. With no `ask`, the lead titles stand in;\n * an empty result still yields a roundup angle so a non-empty intake always\n * produces at least one story. */\nexport async function assignAngles(\n  voice: string,\n  topic: string,\n  items: readonly SyndicationItem[],\n  max = 3,\n  ask?: Ask,\n): Promise<readonly string[]> {\n  const reply = ask ? await ask(assignmentPrompt(voice, topic, items, max)) : items.slice(0, max).map((item) => item.title).join(\"\\n\");\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\n  const angles: string[] = [];\n  for (const angle of parseAngles(reply)) {\n    const key = newsSlug(angle).split(\"-\").slice(0, 8).join(\"-\");\n    if (!key || seen.has(key)) continue;\n    seen.add(key);\n    angles.push(angle);\n    if (angles.length >= max) break;\n  }\n  if (angles.length === 0 && items.length > 0) angles.push(`What's new in ${topic}`);\n  return Object.freeze(angles);\n}\n\n/** Options for the newsroom cycle: the clock stamp, the beat to draw intake\n * from, the assignment topic and story bound, and the cultivation I/O. */\nexport type NewsroomCycleOptions = Readonly<{\n  at: string;\n  beat?: string;\n  topic?: string;\n  maxStories?: number;\n  ask?: Ask;\n  fetchImpl?: FetchLike;\n  adapters?: Readonly<Record<string, SyndicationAdapter>>;\n  dryRun?: boolean;\n  provider?: string;\n  model?: string;\n  env?: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>;\n}>;\n\n/** One newsroom cycle for a property: fetch the beat's intake ONCE, assign the\n * day's angles over it, then run the base cultivation cycle once per angle with\n * the newsroom seams (angle selection, brief composition, assertion-trace\n * recording). The witnessed stories and the per-angle obstructions are both\n * returned as values. */\nexport type NewsroomCycleResult = Readonly<{\n  kind: \"content.farm.newsroom-cycle:witness\";\n  property: string;\n  angles: readonly string[];\n  intakeObstructions: readonly string[];\n  stories: readonly NewsroomCultivation[];\n  obstructions: readonly CultivationObstruction[];\n}>;\n\n/** Run one newsroom cycle. See NewsroomCycleResult. */\nexport async function runNewsroomCycle(property: FarmProperty, options: NewsroomCycleOptions): Promise<NewsroomCycleResult> {\n  const beat = options.beat ?? Object.keys(property.beatSources)[0] ?? \"\";\n  const intake = await intakeItems(property, beat, {\n    ...(options.fetchImpl === undefined ? {} : { fetchImpl: options.fetchImpl }),\n    ...(options.adapters === undefined ? {} : { adapters: options.adapters }),\n  });\n  const topic = options.topic ?? property.termKey ?? property.name;\n  const voice = [...property.voice.persona, ...(property.voice.laws ?? [])].join(\" \");\n  const angles = await assignAngles(voice, topic, intake.items, options.maxStories ?? 3, options.ask);\n  const stories: NewsroomCultivation[] = [];\n  const obstructions: CultivationObstruction[] = [];\n  for (const angle of angles) {\n    const result = await cultivate(property, {\n      at: options.at,\n      term: angle,\n      beat,\n      items: intake.items,\n      ...(options.ask === undefined ? {} : { ask: options.ask }),\n      ...(options.dryRun === undefined ? {} : { dryRun: options.dryRun }),\n      ...(options.provider === undefined ? {} : { provider: options.provider }),\n      ...(options.model === undefined ? {} : { model: options.model }),\n      ...(options.env === undefined ? {} : { env: options.env }),\n      select: newsroomSelect,\n      compose: newsroomCompose,\n      record: newsroomRecord,\n    });\n    if (result.kind === \"content.farm.newsroom-cultivation:witness\") stories.push(result);\n    else obstructions.push(result);\n  }\n  return Object.freeze({\n    kind: \"content.farm.newsroom-cycle:witness\" as const,\n    property: property.name,\n    angles,\n    intakeObstructions: intake.obstructions,\n    stories: Object.freeze(stories),\n    obstructions: Object.freeze(obstructions),\n  });\n}\n"},{"sourceId":"production/article-topology","digest":"sha256:8928087afe878a8fc4534dc392cbd5cc741985bdc1333227bad75957bd93a569","characters":30697,"contentOmitted":"digest-bound pipeline manifest; unrelated full bytes remain customer-side"},{"sourceId":"production/inference-adapter","digest":"sha256:83b521f69a3a1593f76efd6fe3dcdfe5868659c893db1918d5ffe0e4ec634f1f","characters":5595,"content":"/**\n * ask ‚Äî a prompt-to-text morphism over OpenAI-compatible chat completion\n * endpoints.\n *\n * `makeAsk` closes over one provider configuration and returns\n * `(prompt) => Promise<string>`; the production cycle takes that function\n * as a value and never sees a provider. Providers, keys, and `fetch` all\n * enter as values, so consumers and tests can run hermetically.\n *\n * Provider note (carried from operations): `nim` is the default-capable\n * provider (https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions, keyed by\n * NVIDIA_API_KEY). `groq` has a tiny context window and is suitable ONLY\n * for prompts well under 8k tokens.\n */\n\ntype FetchLike = typeof fetch;\n\nexport type ContentProviderName = \"groq\" | \"nim\";\n\nexport type ContentProvider = Readonly<{\n  url: string;\n  keyEnv: string;\n  model: string;\n}>;\n\nexport type ContentProviderUsage = Readonly<{\n  promptTokens?: number;\n  completionTokens?: number;\n  totalTokens?: number;\n  raw?: unknown;\n}>;\n\nexport type ContentAskOptions = Readonly<{\n  provider?: ContentProviderName | string;\n  providers?: Readonly<Record<string, ContentProvider>>;\n  model?: string;\n  temperature?: number;\n  maxTokens?: number;\n  env?: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>;\n  fetchImpl?: FetchLike;\n  onUsage?: (usage: ContentProviderUsage, meta: Readonly<{ provider: string; model: string }>) => void;\n}>;\n\n/**\n * The default provider registry. `nim` is the default-capable provider;\n * `groq` only suits prompts well under 8k tokens (tiny context window).\n */\nexport const contentProviders: Readonly<Record<string, ContentProvider>> = Object.freeze({\n  groq: Object.freeze({ url: \"https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions\", keyEnv: \"GROQ_API_KEY\", model: \"llama-3.1-8b-instant\" }),\n  nim: Object.freeze({ url: \"https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions\", keyEnv: \"NVIDIA_API_KEY\", model: \"meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct\" }),\n});\n\nfunction envValue(env: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>, key: string): string | undefined {\n  const value = env[key];\n  return value === \"\" ? undefined : value;\n}\n\n/** Whether a provider is configured AND keyed in the given environment.\n *  Boolean convenience at the app edge (invariant A1 reserves carriers for\n *  lib judgments; an app may answer configuration questions plainly). */\nexport function hasProvider(provider: string, opts: Pick<ContentAskOptions, \"providers\" | \"env\"> = {}): boolean {\n  const providers = opts.providers ?? contentProviders;\n  const config = providers[provider];\n  return !!(config && envValue(opts.env ?? process.env, config.keyEnv));\n}\n\n/** First keyed provider in preference order; nim leads (see module note). */\nexport function pickProvider(order: readonly string[] = [\"nim\", \"groq\"], opts: Pick<ContentAskOptions, \"providers\" | \"env\"> = {}): string | null {\n  return order.find((provider) => hasProvider(provider, opts)) ?? null;\n}\n\nfunction normalizeProviderUsage(value: unknown): ContentProviderUsage {\n  if (!value || typeof value !== \"object\") return Object.freeze({ raw: value });\n  const usage = value as { prompt_tokens?: unknown; completion_tokens?: unknown; total_tokens?: unknown };\n  const promptTokens = typeof usage.prompt_tokens === \"number\" ? usage.prompt_tokens : undefined;\n  const completionTokens = typeof usage.completion_tokens === \"number\" ? usage.completion_tokens : undefined;\n  const totalTokens = typeof usage.total_tokens === \"number\" ? usage.total_tokens : undefined;\n  const normalized: { promptTokens?: number; completionTokens?: number; totalTokens?: number; raw?: unknown } = { raw: value };\n  if (promptTokens !== undefined) normalized.promptTokens = promptTokens;\n  if (completionTokens !== undefined) normalized.completionTokens = completionTokens;\n  if (totalTokens !== undefined) normalized.totalTokens = totalTokens;\n  return Object.freeze(normalized);\n}\n\n/**\n * Close over one provider configuration and return the ask morphism.\n * Defaults to `nim`, the default-capable provider; pass `provider: \"groq\"`\n * only for prompts well under 8k tokens. Throws only on malformed\n * configuration (unknown provider, unkeyed environment) ‚Äî transport\n * failures surface per call.\n */\nexport function makeAsk(options: ContentAskOptions = {}): (prompt: string) => Promise<string> {\n  const providerName = options.provider ?? \"nim\";\n  const providers = options.providers ?? contentProviders;\n  const provider = providers[providerName];\n  if (!provider) throw new TypeError(`unknown provider \"${providerName}\"`);\n  const key = envValue(options.env ?? process.env, provider.keyEnv);\n  if (!key) throw new TypeError(`${provider.keyEnv} is not set`);\n  const model = options.model ?? provider.model;\n  const fetchImpl = options.fetchImpl ?? fetch;\n  const temperature = options.temperature ?? 0.4;\n  return async (prompt: string): Promise<string> => {\n    const response = await fetchImpl(provider.url, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\", authorization: `Bearer ${key}` },\n      body: JSON.stringify({\n        model,\n        messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: String(prompt) }],\n        temperature,\n        ...(options.maxTokens === undefined ? {} : { max_tokens: options.maxTokens }),\n      }),\n    });\n    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`${providerName} ${model}: HTTP ${response.status}`);\n    const data = await response.json() as { usage?: unknown; choices?: readonly { message?: { content?: unknown } }[] };\n    options.onUsage?.(normalizeProviderUsage(data.usage), { provider: providerName, model });\n    return String(data.choices?.[0]?.message?.content ?? \"\");\n  };\n}\n"}]

